    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Some causes of granulomatous inflammation, with key cytopathological findings {22706525; 26800030; 27555237; 30407860; 26143421; 26143429}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Arvind Rajwanshi",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 658.8pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"878\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.4pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Etiology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Cytopathology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; mso-background-themecolor: text2; mso-background-themetint: 102; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Ancillary tests and comments</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><em>Mycobacterium tuberculosis</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Epithelioid granulomas, giant cells, &plusmn;&nbsp;necrosis, suppurative inflammation, spindle cell pseudotumour</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Acid-fast stains, auramine fluorescence, nucleic acid amplification tests, culture</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Non-tubercular mycobacterial infection, </span></strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">e.g. </span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"><em>Mycobacterium avium</em> complex (MAC)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Epithelioid granulomas, foamy histiocytes, giant cells, &plusmn;&nbsp;necrosis, background showing negative image of bacilli, suppurative inflammation</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Acid-fast stains, auramine fluorescence, PCR, culture</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">BCG lymphadenitis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Sheets of neutrophils, aggregates of foamy macrophages, reactive lymphoid cells, granulomas, giant cells, necrotic background</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Acid-fast stains, auramine fluorescence, PCR, culture; usually, a well child with milestones attained</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Nocardia</span></em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Suppurative/necrotizing inflammation with long, thin, filamentous branching Gram-positive bacilli</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Modified Ziehl&ndash;Neelsen stain (Fite stain) or <span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">Kinyoun</span> stain using 1% sulfuric acid as decolourizer; Gram stain; methenamine silver stain</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Leprosy</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Histiocytes with vacuolated cytoplasm, &plusmn;&nbsp;epithelioid cell collections/granulomas, giant cells; patients with tuberculoid leprosy have a granulomatous response</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Modified Ziehl&ndash;Neelsen stain (e.g. Fite stain)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Rhinoscleroma</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Chronic granulomatous condition caused by <em>Klebsiella rhinoscleromatis</em>; granulomas with or without necrosis; plasma cells; foamy macrophages (Mikulicz cells containing bacteria), fibrosis in late stages</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">DPAS; Giemsa stain; Steiner or Hotchkiss&ndash;McManus stains for Gram-negative bacteria</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Various other bacterial diseases, </strong>e.g. cat-scratch disease, lymphogranuloma venereum, tularaemia, plague, brucellosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Stellate epithelioid granulomas; reactive lymphoid population; tingible-body macrophages; acute inflammation, variable amount of necrosis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Depends on the most likely organism</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Fungi</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><em>Cryptococcus</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Intracellular and/or extracellular teardrop, oval to spherical yeasts (6&ndash;20&nbsp;&mu;m), some showing narrow-necked budding, with a faintly refractile halo of a thick mucopolysaccharide capsule, granulomatous and/or necrotizing inflammatory reaction or no inflammatory response</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive in PAS&ndash;Alcian blue stain; mucicarmine stain; methenamine silver stain; Fontana&ndash;Masson stain; negative image in Indian ink; culture, lateral flow test, antigen titres</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histoplasmosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Spherical to oval, budding yeast, 2&ndash;4&nbsp;&mu;m in diameter, often intracellular within histiocytes; necrosis, fibrosis in later stages</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">DPAS and methenamine silver stain positive; culture, serology</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Blastomyces</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Suppurative granulomas with double-contour, 8&ndash;15&nbsp;&mu;m yeasts showing broad-based budding</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive in DPAS and methenamine; culture, serology</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Coccidioidomycosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Suppurative granulomas with spherules of 40&ndash;100&nbsp;&mu;m with an eosinophilic wall, containing multiple basophilic endospores (2&ndash;5&nbsp;&mu;m)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Positive in DPAS methenamine stain; culture, serology</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><em>Pneumocystis jirovecii</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Small, cup/boat-shaped cysts (4&ndash;6&nbsp;&mu;m) containing a bluish dot in Giemsa stain; rarely with granulomas</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Methenamine stain; Warthin&ndash;Starry stain; immunocytochemistry</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 14; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Leishmaniasis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Macrophages containing <em><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">Leishmania donovani</span></em> (LD) bodies (amastigotes, 2&ndash;4&nbsp;&mu;m oval structures with pale-blue cytoplasm, large dark nucleus, and characteristic kinetoplast), plasma cells</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Giemsa stain, negative for DPAS stain, culture, PCR, serology</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 15; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Toxoplasmosis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Large histiocytes containing bradyzoites, reactive lymphoid population, epithelioid microgranulomas, plasma cells, bradyzoites in background: crescent-shaped organisms within histiocytes and lymphocytes</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Giemsa stain, immunocytochemistry, serology</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 16; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Filariasis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Microfilariae of <em><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">Wuchereria bancrofti</span></em>, with outer sheath and granules that do not extend into the tail of the microfilariae, inflammation including eosinophils and granulomas; the worm and eggs</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Giemsa stain; artefacts such as cotton thread should be excluded</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 17; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Non-infectious</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 18; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Sarcoidosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Non-necrotizing and well-formed granulomas, chronic inflammation, Schaumann and asteroid bodies</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Often involves hilar or mediastinal lymph nodes; mycobacterial infection may need to be actively excluded</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 19; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Foreign body</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Well-formed granulomas, usually non-caseating, foreign-body giant cells, chronic inflammation, fibrosis, may become secondarily infected with bacteria or fungi</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Foreign body can be refractile or polarize, giant cells are CD68-positive on immunocytochemistry</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 20; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Kikuchi&ndash;Fujimoto disease</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Histiocytic cells with crescent-shaped nuclei and eccentric cytoplasm; immunoblasts; absence of neutrophils; necrotic karyorrhectic debris</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Microorganism stains are negative</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 21; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Chronic (septic) granulomatous disease (CGD)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Granulomas with central necrosis; pigment-containing macrophages</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Microorganism stains to exclude specific infection</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 22; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Treatment changes, </span></strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">e.g. radiation, medication</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Usually non-necrotizing granulomas</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; mso-background-themecolor: accent5; mso-background-themetint: 51; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Microorganism stains are negative</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 23; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"26\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 128.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"172\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Malignancy, </strong>e.g. Hodgkin and non-Hodgkin lymphomas, germ cell tumour, metastatic nasopharyngeal carcinoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Malignant cells are present among the granulomas and inflammation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 255.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"340\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Immunocytochemistry and molecular tests, depending on the suspected malignancy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  }
]